{"questions":[{"question_id":"1l1p04tld","paperTitle":"JEE Advanced 2013 Paper 1 Offline","year":2013,"examDate":2013,"subject":"chemistry","chapter":"solid-state","chapterGroup":"physical-chemistry","topic":"structure-of-ionic-compounds","type":"mcq","marks":3,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"pthe-arrangement-of-xsup-sup-ions-around-asup-jee-advanced-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-sfda8hj5mxz2pbxx","content":"<p>The arrangement of X<sup><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></sup> ions around A<sup>+</sup> ion in solid AX is given in the figure (not drawn to scale). If the radius of X<sup><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></sup> is 250 pm, the radius of A<sup>+</sup> is</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l1tvt9pq/4adf1917-cb35-40ab-a1f9-23fa9e6b6a0d/f92471d0-b920-11ec-aba9-13802b916eff/file-1l1tvt9pr.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l1tvt9pq/4adf1917-cb35-40ab-a1f9-23fa9e6b6a0d/f92471d0-b920-11ec-aba9-13802b916eff/file-1l1tvt9pr.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2013 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - Solid State Question 15 English\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l1tvt9pq/4adf1917-cb35-40ab-a1f9-23fa9e6b6a0d/f92471d0-b920-11ec-aba9-13802b916eff/file-1l1tvt9pr.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l1tvt9pq/4adf1917-cb35-40ab-a1f9-23fa9e6b6a0d/f92471d0-b920-11ec-aba9-13802b916eff/file-1l1tvt9pr.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l1tvt9pq/4adf1917-cb35-40ab-a1f9-23fa9e6b6a0d/f92471d0-b920-11ec-aba9-13802b916eff/file-1l1tvt9pr.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l1tvt9pq/4adf1917-cb35-40ab-a1f9-23fa9e6b6a0d/f92471d0-b920-11ec-aba9-13802b916eff/file-1l1tvt9pr.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l1tvt9pq/4adf1917-cb35-40ab-a1f9-23fa9e6b6a0d/f92471d0-b920-11ec-aba9-13802b916eff/file-1l1tvt9pr.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l1tvt9pq/4adf1917-cb35-40ab-a1f9-23fa9e6b6a0d/f92471d0-b920-11ec-aba9-13802b916eff/file-1l1tvt9pr.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"104 pm"},{"identifier":"B","content":"125 pm"},{"identifier":"C","content":"183 pm"},{"identifier":"D","content":"57 pm"}],"correct_options":["A"],"explanation":"<p>From the figure, it can be seen that the cation A<sup>+</sup> occupies octahedral void formed by the anion X<sup><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></sup>. The radius ratio for an octahedral void is r<sub>A<sup>+</sup></sub> / r<sub>X<sup><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></sup></sub> = 0.414. Now, given that the radius of anion X<sup><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></sup> is 250 pm, so the radius of A<sup>+</sup> is</p>\n<p>r<sub>A<sup>+</sup></sub> = 0.414 <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0.02ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.09ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -491 778 482\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"D7\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-D7\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> 250 = 103.50 <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0.081ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"0.968ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -464 778 428\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2243\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2243\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> 104 pm</p>"}]}